next door, which is why this file exists separately rather than being cross-referenced.

This directory is the CONTROL arm. Its rules.yaml sets IntelSampleInterval: 999999 on
DroneOperatorBotModule@experimental, which is the feature's documented off switch
(DroneOperatorBotModule.cs:108-116): SampleIntel never runs, the contact table is never
written, BestIntelAt returns 0 for every candidate, and the drone is tasked on revealed-area
staleness alone. A drone that cannot know where the enemy was last seen has no way to prefer
that cell, so FAIL is the only outcome this arm can honestly produce. A PASS here is loudly
RED: it means either the override did not merge (see below) or the drone reached the vanish
cell by exploration geometry alone, and CONTROL-ARM.md says to REPORT AND STOP on that second
case rather than re-running or moving the threshold.

THE ONE FAILURE THIS DECLARATION MUST NOT ABSORB, because it produces the declared outcome
